Problem:

The internal shop site is down. The requirement is simple:
curl http://shop.internal:8080/
must return the shop page over plain HTTP on port 8080.
This is the intended architecture on this machine:
   . The name shop.internal resolves to 127.0.0.1 through an entry in /etc/hosts.
   . nginx listens on port 8080 with a server block at /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/shop that proxies every request to the backend at http://127.0.0.1:9000.
   . The backend is a Python http.server process serving the directory /opt/shop/www on port 9000. The page it serves contains the text Welcome to the shop.
   . No firewall rule blocks traffic to port 8080.
Right now more than one thing is broken, and the faults are independent: fixing one does not fix the others. Find every fault, fix it, and verify the site end to end.


Solution:

1. Interface, IP address, and routing: ip link, ip addr, ip route, ip route show table local
   Verified that the loopback interface was UP, 127.0.0.1 was assigned, and the local and default routes existed.
2. Check listening ports and processes
   Found that the required backend port 9000 was not listening
3. Start the Python backend on port 9000
   CMD: python3 -m http.server 9000 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory /opt/shop/www > /tmp/shop-backend.log 2>&1 &
   Verify the backend: curl http://127.0.0.1:9000/ Output: Welcome to the shop
4. Check and fix the firewall
   CMD: iptables -L -n
   Found a DROP rule blocking TCP port 8080. Removed it
   CMD: iptables -D INPUT -p tcp --dport 8080 -j DROP
5. Fix hostname resolution
   Updated the /etc/hosts shop.internal resolves to 127.0.0.1
6. Validate and start nginx
   It was disabled, and I activated nginx
   CMD: systemctl start nginx
   The intended nginx configuration in /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/shop proxies requests to http://127.0.0.1:9000
7. Final verification
   curl -v http://shop.internal:8080/ 
   Output: Welcome to the shop
